  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Oral bioavailability is about 100%, and a high-fat meal makes no clinically significant difference to exposure. It is 96% protein bound and mainly metabolized by CYP2C8 and CYP3A4.",
    "substance": "The active ingredient has a molecular weight of 477.44 and is practically insoluble in aqueous media across a wide pH range.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 60 mg and 240 mg tablets, taken once daily.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning and no contraindications. Fatigue and arthralgia are among the most common adverse reactions, and severe skin reactions are a warning.",
    "indication": "Metastatic castration-sensitive prostate cancer and non-metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer.",
    "mechanism": "Binds the androgen receptor's ligand-binding domain, blocking its nuclear translocation, DNA binding and transcription."
  },
  "tell": "An androgen receptor inhibitor whose N-desmethyl metabolite likely adds to its clinical activity, with a half-life near 3 days.",
